A||||3||fierosound||Bonneville wheels - will they fit||||5||
Z||000000||fierosound||04-29-2000||12:06 PM||||I've seen Bonnevilles driving around on what appear to be 16" versions of the Fiero Diamond Spoke alloy wheels.  I've seen them with black or gold centers.  I know they are 16"x7" wheels, but nothing else, such as bolt circle or offset.  Does anyone know if these will fit Fieros?  If not a direct fit, what would be required (coilovers, spacers) etc.???  Thanks... <P><BR>Photo of Bonneville with these wheels at link below: <BR><A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=316806940" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=316806940</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 04-29-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-29-2000||01:40 PM||||Don't know but this may help:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/wheels.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/wheels.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-29-2000||02:35 PM||||No they won't fit. Fiero is 5 X 100mm Bonneville's are 5 X 110mm.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||04-30-2000||12:06 PM||||Thanks Dad...  I'd seen the list before and noticed the Bonneville wheels weren't there.  I wasn't sure if the new Bonne wheels would fit.  Thanks Oreif for giving us a definite answer and clearing this up.  I guess redrilling the hubs would be required to use them! <P>I've seen some Grand Prixs with similar wheels, and they are on the list.  I suppose they should fit with proper backspacing.  Now it's a matter of finding a set of those...<P>I'd like to go to 16" wheels, but would like the wheels with the "same look" of the Fiero's original Diamond Spoke wheels.  Anyone have any ideas as to what looks similar and may fit?? ||||reg||10
